I'll reveal this.

00:23:30.515 --> 00:23:32.640
The first part is essentially
getting your data in,

00:23:32.640 --> 00:23:34.080
so get help KPIs.

00:23:34.080 --> 00:23:37.050
It's a helper function that's
sourced in from these other R

00:23:37.050 --> 00:23:38.640
script files.

00:23:38.640 --> 00:23:41.460
And this just gets us
our data to work with.

00:23:44.393 --> 00:23:45.810
And in different
circumstances, it

00:23:45.810 --> 00:23:47.180
could be pulling
in database data,

00:23:47.180 --> 00:23:49.597
it could be pulling in data
from an Excel sheet, whatever.

00:23:49.597 --> 00:23:53.140
The idea is just to get
the data into this report.

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:56.450
And then we can apply
other functions.

00:23:56.450 --> 00:24:00.210
What we're doing now, is
we're transforming the data.

00:24:00.210 --> 00:24:02.383
And then we have a
set of thresholds.

00:24:02.383 --> 00:24:03.800
And what we're
doing with that, is

00:24:03.800 --> 00:24:06.094
we're saying that
for each these KPIs,

00:24:06.094 --> 00:24:10.190
this one is daily active
users, daily active customers.

00:24:10.190 --> 00:24:14.030
We have new users, returned
users, and daily revenue,

00:24:14.030 --> 00:24:16.370
and a ratio of DAC over DAU.

00:24:16.370 --> 00:24:21.940
And we're saying that,
if there's an exceedance,

00:24:21.940 --> 00:24:23.440
this will be less
than the threshold

